/-!
# Global types of modules on a ringed topos, and their pullback

Stacks 03DE lists seven global conditions on a sheaf of modules `F` over a sheaf of rings `O`:
being free, finite free, generated by global sections, generated by `r` global sections,
generated by finitely many global sections, having a global presentation and having a finite
global presentation.  Stacks 03DF says that each of them is carried by the pullback
`f^*F = O_C ⊗_{f⁻¹O_D} f⁻¹F` of Stacks 03D6 (2) along a morphism of ringed topoi
`(f, f♯) : (Sh(C), O_C) ⟶ (Sh(D), O_D)`, because `f^*` commutes with arbitrary colimits
(Stacks 03DC) and `f^*O_D = O_C`.

Five of the seven conditions are defined here; the other two are already in the library, where
they support the local conditions of Stacks 03DL, and are registered against 03DE at the end of
this file, together with the library's own forms of conditions (6) and (7).

## Main definitions

* `SheafOfModules.IsFree` is Stacks 03DE (1): the module is a coproduct of copies of the
  structure sheaf.
* `SheafOfModules.IsGeneratedByGlobalSections` is Stacks 03DE (3): some family of global
  sections generates the module.
* `SheafOfModules.IsGeneratedByGlobalSectionsOfCard` is Stacks 03DE (4): some family of
  global sections indexed by a type with `r` elements generates the module.
* `SheafOfModules.IsPresentedByGlobalSections` is Stacks 03DE (6): the module is a cokernel of
  a map between two coproducts of copies of the structure sheaf.
* `SheafOfModules.IsFinitelyPresentedByGlobalSections` is Stacks 03DE (7): the two coproducts
  of such a presentation can be taken finite.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedToposHom.pullbackModulesFreeIso`: the pullback of the free module on
  a type is the free module on the same type.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedToposHom.generatingSectionsPullbackModules`: a generating family of
  global sections, pulled back to a generating family indexed by the same type.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedToposHom.isColimitCofanPullbackModules`: a module written as a
  coproduct of copies of `O_D` pulls back to the coproduct of the same number of copies of
  `O_C`.  This is the colimit computation all of Stacks 03DF rests on.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedToposHom.pullbackModules_isFree`,
  `.pullbackModules_isFiniteFree`,
  `.pullbackModules_isPresentedByGlobalSections` and
  `.pullbackModules_isFinitelyPresentedByGlobalSections`: **Stacks 03DF, clauses (1), (2), (6)
  and (7)**, the four that need no sheafification on the target.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedToposHom.pullbackModules_isGeneratedByGlobalSections`,
  `.pullbackModules_isGeneratedByGlobalSectionsOfCard` and
  `.pullbackModules_exists_isGeneratedByGlobalSectionsOfCard`: **Stacks 03DF, clauses
  (3)–(5).**
* `SheafOfModules.isPresentedByGlobalSections_iff_hasGlobalPresentation` and
  `.isFinitelyPresentedByGlobalSections_iff_hasFiniteGlobalPresentation`: the two conditions
  defined here agree with the library's `SheafOfModules.HasGlobalPresentation` and
  `SheafOfModules.HasFiniteGlobalPresentation` at the universe of sections where both are
  stated.

## Implementation notes

The conditions defined here are stated in the shape in which their local counterparts of
Stacks 03DL inline them in `StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Topologies.ModuleTypesOnSite`:
freeness and the two presentation conditions through the universal properties of a coproduct of
copies of `SheafOfModules.unit` and of a cokernel, and the two generation conditions through
Mathlib's `SheafOfModules.GeneratingSections`.  So
`SheafOfModules.IsLocallyFreeOnSite`, `SheafOfModules.IsLocallyGeneratedBySectionsOnSite` and
`SheafOfModules.IsLocallyGeneratedByOnSite` are literally the assertion that the corresponding
condition here holds on the members of a covering.  `SheafOfModules.IsGeneratedBy` is the
unrelated, more general condition that some coproduct of copies of a *given* module surjects
onto the module; clause (3) is its instance at the structure sheaf.

The two ringed topoi are given the same universe of sections.  This is forced by the
statements and not by their proofs: a free module on the target is free on an index type
living in the universe of sections of the target, and the pullback must be free on an index
type living in that of the source, so with independent universes there is no index type to
transport.

The library's `SheafOfModules.HasGlobalPresentation` and
`SheafOfModules.HasFiniteGlobalPresentation` place the two coproducts and the module in the
universe `max u v w m` built from the site, the coefficient ring and the module, whereas the
pullback functor of Stacks 03D6 (2) acts on the module universe `w` of the ringed topos, and the
two site universes of the source and of the target differ.  So clauses (6) and (7) are stated
here for `SheafOfModules.IsPresentedByGlobalSections` and
`SheafOfModules.IsFinitelyPresentedByGlobalSections`, which repeat those two conditions with the
universe lift removed, and `SheafOfModules.isPresentedByGlobalSections_iff_hasGlobalPresentation`
and `SheafOfModules.isFinitelyPresentedByGlobalSections_iff_hasFiniteGlobalPresentation` record
that nothing is lost: over a ring sheaf and a module whose sections already contain the site, the
universe lift is an isomorphism and the two conditions are equivalent.

Clauses (6) and (7) precede clauses (3)–(5) here because, like clauses (1) and (2), they are
proved from colimits alone and so hold without the sheafification hypotheses on the target
topos that `SheafOfModules.GeneratingSections` carries.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DE](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DE)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DF](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DF)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DC](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DC)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03D6](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03D6)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits AlgebraicGeometry
open Stacks.Sheaves.RingedToposModules

namespace SheafOfModules

universe w v u

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C} {R : Sheaf J RingCat.{w}}

/-- A sheaf of modules is **free** when it is a coproduct of copies of the structure sheaf,
that is, when some family of global sections exhibits it as such a coproduct.  The coproduct
is specified by its universal property, so no sheafification instance is needed.  This is
Stacks 03DE (1). -/
@[stacks 03DE "free"]
def IsFree (F : SheafOfModules.{w} R) : Prop :=
  ∃ (B : Type w) (ι : ∀ _ : B, SheafOfModules.unit R ⟶ F),
    Nonempty (IsColimit (Cofan.mk F ι))

/-- Local freeness is freeness on the members of a covering of every object. -/
theorem isLocallyFreeOnSite_iff_isFree (F : SheafOfModules.{w} R) :
    IsLocallyFreeOnSite F ↔
      ∀ U : C, ∃ (I : Type (max u v)) (V : I → C) (f : ∀ i, V i ⟶ U),
        (Sieve.ofArrows V f ∈ J U) ∧ ∀ i : I, IsFree (F.over (V i)) :=
  Iff.rfl

/-- A sheaf of modules **has a global presentation** when it is a cokernel of a map between two
coproducts of copies of the structure sheaf, that is, when it is the right-hand term of an exact
sequence `⊕_{j ∈ K} O ⟶ ⊕_{i ∈ I} O ⟶ F ⟶ 0`.  The coproducts and the cokernel are specified by
their universal properties, so no sheafification instance is needed.  This is Stacks 03DE (6). -/
@[stacks 03DE "global presentation, at a single universe of sections"]
def IsPresentedByGlobalSections (F : SheafOfModules.{w} R) : Prop :=
  ∃ (I K : Type w) (P Q : SheafOfModules.{w} R)
    (ι : ∀ _ : I, SheafOfModules.unit R ⟶ P) (κ : ∀ _ : K, SheafOfModules.unit R ⟶ Q),
    Nonempty (IsColimit (Cofan.mk P ι)) ∧ Nonempty (IsColimit (Cofan.mk Q κ)) ∧
      ∃ (a : Q ⟶ P) (b : P ⟶ F) (hab : a ≫ b = 0),
        Nonempty (IsColimit (CokernelCofork.ofπ b hab))

/-- A sheaf of modules **has a finite global presentation** when it is a cokernel of a map
between two *finite* coproducts of copies of the structure sheaf, that is, when it is the
right-hand term of an exact sequence `O^{⊕k} ⟶ O^{⊕n} ⟶ F ⟶ 0`.  This is Stacks 03DE (7). -/
@[stacks 03DE "finite global presentation, at a single universe of sections"]
def IsFinitelyPresentedByGlobalSections (F : SheafOfModules.{w} R) : Prop :=
  ∃ (n k : ℕ) (P Q : SheafOfModules.{w} R)
    (ι : ∀ _ : Fin n, SheafOfModules.unit R ⟶ P) (κ : ∀ _ : Fin k, SheafOfModules.unit R ⟶ Q),
    Nonempty (IsColimit (Cofan.mk P ι)) ∧ Nonempty (IsColimit (Cofan.mk Q κ)) ∧
      ∃ (a : Q ⟶ P) (b : P ⟶ F) (hab : a ≫ b = 0),
        Nonempty (IsColimit (CokernelCofork.ofπ b hab))

/-- A module with a finite global presentation has a global presentation: the two finite index
types are reindexed by their universe lifts. -/
theorem IsFinitelyPresentedByGlobalSections.isPresentedByGlobalSections
    {F : SheafOfModules.{w} R} (h : F.IsFinitelyPresentedByGlobalSections) :
    F.IsPresentedByGlobalSections := by
  obtain ⟨n, k, P, Q, ι, κ, ⟨hP⟩, ⟨hQ⟩, a, b, hab, hc⟩ := h
  exact ⟨ULift.{w} (Fin n), ULift.{w} (Fin k), P, Q, fun i ↦ ι i.down, fun i ↦ κ i.down,
    ⟨(Cofan.isColimitEquivOfEquiv Equiv.ulift (Cofan.mk P ι)) hP⟩,
    ⟨(Cofan.isColimitEquivOfEquiv Equiv.ulift (Cofan.mk Q κ)) hQ⟩, a, b, hab, hc⟩

/-- A presentation by coproducts of copies of `U` and a cokernel transfers along isomorphisms of
the summand `U` and of the cokernel `F`. -/
private theorem exists_presentation_of_iso {I K : Type*} {U U' F F' : SheafOfModules.{w} R}
    (eU : U' ≅ U) (eF : F' ≅ F)
    (h : ∃ (P Q : SheafOfModules.{w} R) (ι : I → (U ⟶ P)) (κ : K → (U ⟶ Q)),
      Nonempty (IsColimit (Cofan.mk P ι)) ∧ Nonempty (IsColimit (Cofan.mk Q κ)) ∧
        ∃ (a : Q ⟶ P) (b : P ⟶ F) (hab : a ≫ b = 0),
          Nonempty (IsColimit (CokernelCofork.ofπ b hab))) :
    ∃ (P Q : SheafOfModules.{w} R) (ι : I → (U' ⟶ P)) (κ : K → (U' ⟶ Q)),
      Nonempty (IsColimit (Cofan.mk P ι)) ∧ Nonempty (IsColimit (Cofan.mk Q κ)) ∧
        ∃ (a : Q ⟶ P) (b : P ⟶ F') (hab : a ≫ b = 0),
          Nonempty (IsColimit (CokernelCofork.ofπ b hab)) := by
  obtain ⟨P, Q, ι, κ, ⟨hP⟩, ⟨hQ⟩, a, b, hab, ⟨hc⟩⟩ := h
  exact ⟨P, Q, fun i ↦ eU.hom ≫ ι i, fun i ↦ eU.hom ≫ κ i,
    ⟨isColimit_cofan_comp_iso eU ι hP⟩, ⟨isColimit_cofan_comp_iso eU κ hQ⟩, a, b ≫ eF.inv,
    by rw [← Category.assoc, hab, zero_comp], ⟨hc.ofIsoColimit (Cofork.ext eF.symm rfl)⟩⟩

section UniverseComparison

variable {R' : Sheaf J RingCat.{max u v w}}

/-- The global presentations of Stacks 03DE (6) at a single universe of sections are those of
`SheafOfModules.HasGlobalPresentation`, at the universe where the two agree: the sections of the
module and of the structure sheaf already contain the site, so the universe lift that the latter
takes first is an isomorphism. -/
theorem isPresentedByGlobalSections_iff_hasGlobalPresentation
    (F : SheafOfModules.{max u v w} R') :
    F.IsPresentedByGlobalSections ↔ F.HasGlobalPresentation := by
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨I, K, h⟩
    exact ⟨I, K, exists_presentation_of_iso (uliftForPresentationSelfIso _)
      (uliftForPresentationSelfIso F) h⟩
  · rintro ⟨I, K, h⟩
    exact ⟨I, K, exists_presentation_of_iso (uliftForPresentationSelfIso _).symm
      (uliftForPresentationSelfIso F).symm h⟩

/-- The finite global presentations of Stacks 03DE (7) at a single universe of sections are those
of `SheafOfModules.HasFiniteGlobalPresentation`, at the universe where the two agree.  The index
types `Fin n` and `Fin k` are the same on both sides; only the universe lift of the structure
sheaf and of the module has to be undone. -/
theorem isFinitelyPresentedByGlobalSections_iff_hasFiniteGlobalPresentation
    (F : SheafOfModules.{max u v w} R') :
    F.IsFinitelyPresentedByGlobalSections ↔ F.HasFiniteGlobalPresentation := by
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨n, k, h⟩
    exact ⟨n, k, exists_presentation_of_iso (uliftForPresentationSelfIso _)
      (uliftForPresentationSelfIso F) h⟩
  · rintro ⟨n, k, h⟩
    exact ⟨n, k, exists_presentation_of_iso (uliftForPresentationSelfIso _).symm
      (uliftForPresentationSelfIso F).symm h⟩

end UniverseComparison

variable [HasWeakSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{w}] [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{w}]

/-- A sheaf of modules is **generated by global sections** when some family of global sections
generates it, that is, when it admits a surjection from a free module.  This is
Stacks 03DE (3). -/
@[stacks 03DE "generated by global sections", ega "0 5.1.1", sga "6 II 2.1.1"]
def IsGeneratedByGlobalSections (F : SheafOfModules.{w} R) : Prop :=
  Nonempty F.GeneratingSections

/-- A sheaf of modules is **generated by `r` global sections** when some family of global
sections indexed by a type with `r` elements generates it, that is, when it admits a surjection
from the free module on such a type.  This is Stacks 03DE (4). -/
@[stacks 03DE "generated by r global sections"]
def IsGeneratedByGlobalSectionsOfCard (F : SheafOfModules.{w} R) (r : ℕ) : Prop :=
  ∃ σ : F.GeneratingSections, Nonempty (σ.I ≃ Fin r)

/-- A module generated by `r` global sections is generated by global sections. -/
theorem IsGeneratedByGlobalSectionsOfCard.isGeneratedByGlobalSections
    {F : SheafOfModules.{w} R} {r : ℕ} (h : F.IsGeneratedByGlobalSectionsOfCard r) :
    F.IsGeneratedByGlobalSections :=
  ⟨h.choose⟩

end SheafOfModules

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.RingedToposHom

universe v u v' u' w t

variable {X : RingedTopos.{v, u, w}} {Y : RingedTopos.{v', u', w}}
  [X.J.HasSheafCompose (forget₂ CommRingCat.{w} RingCat.{w})]
  [Y.J.HasSheafCompose (forget₂ CommRingCat.{w} RingCat.{w})]
  [X.J.HasSheafCompose (forget RingCat.{w})]
  [Y.J.HasSheafCompose (forget RingCat.{w})]
  [X.J.HasSheafCompose (forget AddCommGrpCat.{w})]
  [Y.J.HasSheafCompose (forget AddCommGrpCat.{w})]
  [HasWeakSheafify X.J AddCommGrpCat.{w}]
  [X.J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{w}]

/-- **The colimit computation behind Stacks 03DF.**  A family of global sections exhibiting a
sheaf of `O_D`-modules as a coproduct of copies of `O_D` pulls back to a family exhibiting
`f^*F` as a coproduct of copies of `O_C` indexed by the same type: the pullback commutes with
coproducts (Stacks 03DC) and carries `O_D` to `O_C`. -/
def isColimitCofanPullbackModules (f : RingedToposHom X Y) {B : Type t}
    {F : SheafOfModules.{w} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf (J := Y.J)) Y.O)}
    (ι : ∀ _ : B, SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf (J := Y.J)) Y.O) ⟶ F)
    (h : IsColimit (Cofan.mk F ι)) :
    IsColimit (Cofan.mk ((f.toModulesHom.pullbackModules).obj F)
      (fun b ↦ (pullbackModulesObjUnitIso f.toModulesHom).hom ≫
        (f.toModulesHom.pullbackModules).map (ι b))) :=
  have := pullbackModules_preservesColimitsOfSize.{_, _, _, _, _, _, t, t} f
  ((IsColimit.precomposeHomEquiv
      (Discrete.natIso
        (F := Discrete.functor fun _ : B ↦
          SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf (J := X.J)) X.O))
        (G := Discrete.functor (fun _ : B ↦
          SheafOfModules.unit (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O)) ⋙
            f.toModulesHom.pullbackModules)
        fun _ ↦ pullbackModulesObjUnitIso f.toModulesHom)
      ((f.toModulesHom.pullbackModules).mapCocone (Cofan.mk F ι))).symm
    (isColimitOfPreserves (f.toModulesHom.pullbackModules) h))

/-- The pullback of sheaves of modules along a morphism of ringed topoi preserves
epimorphisms, being a left adjoint. -/
theorem pullbackModules_preservesEpimorphisms (f : RingedToposHom X Y) :
    (f.toModulesHom.pullbackModules).PreservesEpimorphisms :=
  have := pullbackModules_preservesFiniteColimits f
  inferInstance

/-- **Stacks 03DF (1).**  The pullback of a free sheaf of modules along a morphism of ringed
topoi is free. -/
@[stacks 03DF "pullback of a free module is free"]
theorem pullbackModules_isFree (f : RingedToposHom X Y)
    {F : SheafOfModules.{w} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O)} (hF : F.IsFree) :
    ((f.toModulesHom.pullbackModules).obj F).IsFree := by
  obtain ⟨B, ι, ⟨h⟩⟩ := hF
  exact ⟨B, fun b ↦ (pullbackModulesObjUnitIso f.toModulesHom).hom ≫
    (f.toModulesHom.pullbackModules).map (ι b), ⟨isColimitCofanPullbackModules f ι h⟩⟩

/-- **Stacks 03DF (2).**  The pullback of a finite free sheaf of modules along a morphism of
ringed topoi is finite free. -/
@[stacks 03DF "pullback of a finite free module is finite free"]
theorem pullbackModules_isFiniteFree (f : RingedToposHom X Y)
    {F : SheafOfModules.{w} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O)}
    (hF : SheafOfModules.IsFiniteFree (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O) F) :
    SheafOfModules.IsFiniteFree (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)
      ((f.toModulesHom.pullbackModules).obj F) := by
  obtain ⟨n, ι, ⟨h⟩⟩ := (SheafOfModules.isFiniteFree_iff_exists_isColimit _ F).1 hF
  exact (SheafOfModules.isFiniteFree_iff_exists_isColimit _ _).2
    ⟨n, fun b ↦ (pullbackModulesObjUnitIso f.toModulesHom).hom ≫
      (f.toModulesHom.pullbackModules).map (ι b), ⟨isColimitCofanPullbackModules f ι h⟩⟩

/-- The pullback of a presentation by coproducts of copies of `O_D` and a cokernel is a
presentation by coproducts of the same number of copies of `O_C` and a cokernel. -/
private theorem pullbackModules_exists_presentation (f : RingedToposHom X Y) {I K : Type t}
    {F : SheafOfModules.{w} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf (J := Y.J)) Y.O)}
    (h : ∃ (P Q : SheafOfModules.{w} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf (J := Y.J)) Y.O))
      (ι : I → (SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf (J := Y.J)) Y.O) ⟶ P))
      (κ : K → (SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf (J := Y.J)) Y.O) ⟶ Q)),
      Nonempty (IsColimit (Cofan.mk P ι)) ∧ Nonempty (IsColimit (Cofan.mk Q κ)) ∧
        ∃ (a : Q ⟶ P) (b : P ⟶ F) (hab : a ≫ b = 0),
          Nonempty (IsColimit (CokernelCofork.ofπ b hab))) :
    ∃ (P Q : SheafOfModules.{w} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf (J := X.J)) X.O))
      (ι : I → (SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf (J := X.J)) X.O) ⟶ P))
      (κ : K → (SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf (J := X.J)) X.O) ⟶ Q)),
      Nonempty (IsColimit (Cofan.mk P ι)) ∧ Nonempty (IsColimit (Cofan.mk Q κ)) ∧
        ∃ (a : Q ⟶ P) (b : P ⟶ (f.toModulesHom.pullbackModules).obj F) (hab : a ≫ b = 0),
          Nonempty (IsColimit (CokernelCofork.ofπ b hab)) := by
  obtain ⟨P, Q, ι, κ, ⟨hP⟩, ⟨hQ⟩, a, b, hab, ⟨hc⟩⟩ := h
  have := pullbackModules_preservesFiniteColimits f
  exact ⟨(f.toModulesHom.pullbackModules).obj P, (f.toModulesHom.pullbackModules).obj Q,
    fun i ↦ (pullbackModulesObjUnitIso f.toModulesHom).hom ≫
      (f.toModulesHom.pullbackModules).map (ι i),
    fun i ↦ (pullbackModulesObjUnitIso f.toModulesHom).hom ≫
      (f.toModulesHom.pullbackModules).map (κ i),
    ⟨isColimitCofanPullbackModules f ι hP⟩, ⟨isColimitCofanPullbackModules f κ hQ⟩,
    (f.toModulesHom.pullbackModules).map a, (f.toModulesHom.pullbackModules).map b, _,
    ⟨isColimitCoforkMapOfIsColimit' (f.toModulesHom.pullbackModules) hab hc⟩⟩

/-- **Stacks 03DF (6).**  The pullback along a morphism of ringed topoi of a sheaf of modules
with a global presentation has a global presentation: the pullback carries the two coproducts of
copies of `O_D` to coproducts of as many copies of `O_C`, and being right exact it carries the
cokernel to a cokernel. -/
@[stacks 03DF "pullback of a module with a global presentation"]
theorem pullbackModules_isPresentedByGlobalSections (f : RingedToposHom X Y)
    {F : SheafOfModules.{w} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O)}
    (hF : F.IsPresentedByGlobalSections) :
    ((f.toModulesHom.pullbackModules).obj F).IsPresentedByGlobalSections := by
  obtain ⟨I, K, h⟩ := hF
  exact ⟨I, K, pullbackModules_exists_presentation f h⟩

/-- **Stacks 03DF (7).**  The pullback along a morphism of ringed topoi of a sheaf of modules
with a finite global presentation has a finite global presentation: the pulled-back presentation
has the same two finite index types. -/
@[stacks 03DF "pullback of a module with a finite global presentation"]
theorem pullbackModules_isFinitelyPresentedByGlobalSections (f : RingedToposHom X Y)
    {F : SheafOfModules.{w} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf (J := Y.J)) Y.O)}
    (hF : F.IsFinitelyPresentedByGlobalSections) :
    ((f.toModulesHom.pullbackModules).obj F).IsFinitelyPresentedByGlobalSections := by
  obtain ⟨n, k, h⟩ := hF
  exact ⟨n, k, pullbackModules_exists_presentation f h⟩

variable [HasWeakSheafify Y.J AddCommGrpCat.{w}]
  [Y.J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{w}]

/-- **The free comparison of Stacks 03DF.**  The pullback along a morphism of ringed topoi of
the free `O_D`-module on a type is the free `O_C`-module on the same type. -/
def pullbackModulesFreeIso (f : RingedToposHom X Y) (B : Type w) :
    SheafOfModules.free (R := Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O) B ≅
      (f.toModulesHom.pullbackModules).obj (SheafOfModules.free B) :=
  (SheafOfModules.isColimitFreeCofan B).coconePointUniqueUpToIso
    (isColimitCofanPullbackModules f _ (SheafOfModules.isColimitFreeCofan B))

/-- A family of global sections generating a sheaf of `O_D`-modules, pulled back to a family
of global sections generating `f^*F` indexed by the same type.  The generating map is the free
comparison followed by the pullback of the original generating map. -/
def generatingSectionsPullbackModules (f : RingedToposHom X Y)
    {F : SheafOfModules.{w} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O)}
    (σ : F.GeneratingSections) :
    ((f.toModulesHom.pullbackModules).obj F).GeneratingSections where
  I := σ.I
  s := ((f.toModulesHom.pullbackModules).obj F).freeHomEquiv
    ((pullbackModulesFreeIso f σ.I).hom ≫ (f.toModulesHom.pullbackModules).map σ.π)
  epi := by
    have := pullbackModules_preservesEpimorphisms f
    simp only [Equiv.symm_apply_apply, epi_comp_iff_of_epi]
    infer_instance

/-- **Stacks 03DF (3).**  The pullback along a morphism of ringed topoi of a sheaf of modules
generated by global sections is generated by global sections. -/
@[stacks 03DF "pullback of a module generated by global sections"]
theorem pullbackModules_isGeneratedByGlobalSections (f : RingedToposHom X Y)
    {F : SheafOfModules.{w} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O)}
    (hF : F.IsGeneratedByGlobalSections) :
    ((f.toModulesHom.pullbackModules).obj F).IsGeneratedByGlobalSections :=
  ⟨generatingSectionsPullbackModules f hF.some⟩

/-- **Stacks 03DF (4).**  The pullback along a morphism of ringed topoi of a sheaf of modules
generated by `r` global sections is generated by `r` global sections: the pulled-back
generating family is indexed by the same type. -/
@[stacks 03DF "pullback of a module generated by r global sections"]
theorem pullbackModules_isGeneratedByGlobalSectionsOfCard (f : RingedToposHom X Y)
    {F : SheafOfModules.{w} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf (J := Y.J)) Y.O)} {r : ℕ}
    (hF : F.IsGeneratedByGlobalSectionsOfCard r) :
    ((f.toModulesHom.pullbackModules).obj F).IsGeneratedByGlobalSectionsOfCard r :=
  ⟨generatingSectionsPullbackModules f hF.choose, hF.choose_spec⟩

/-- **Stacks 03DF (5).**  The pullback along a morphism of ringed topoi of a sheaf of modules
generated by finitely many global sections is generated by finitely many global sections. -/
@[stacks 03DF "pullback of a module generated by finitely many global sections"]
theorem pullbackModules_exists_isGeneratedByGlobalSectionsOfCard (f : RingedToposHom X Y)
    {F : SheafOfModules.{w} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf (J := Y.J)) Y.O)}
    (hF : ∃ r : ℕ, F.IsGeneratedByGlobalSectionsOfCard r) :
    ∃ r : ℕ, ((f.toModulesHom.pullbackModules).obj F).IsGeneratedByGlobalSectionsOfCard r :=
  ⟨hF.choose, pullbackModules_isGeneratedByGlobalSectionsOfCard f hF.choose_spec⟩

end AlgebraicGeometry.RingedToposHom

-- Clause (2) of Stacks 03DE, finite freeness, is `SheafOfModules.IsFiniteFree`: the module is
-- a coproduct of finitely many copies of the structure sheaf.
add_to_stacks 03DE "finite free" SheafOfModules.IsFiniteFree

-- Clause (5) of Stacks 03DE, generation by finitely many global sections, is
-- `SheafOfModules.HasFiniteGlobalGenerators`: the module admits a surjection from a coproduct
-- of finitely many copies of the structure sheaf.
add_to_stacks 03DE "generated by finitely many global sections"
  SheafOfModules.HasFiniteGlobalGenerators

-- Clause (6) of Stacks 03DE, having a global presentation, is
-- `SheafOfModules.HasGlobalPresentation`: the module is the cokernel of a map between two
-- coproducts of copies of the structure sheaf.
add_to_stacks 03DE "global presentation" SheafOfModules.HasGlobalPresentation

-- Clause (7) of Stacks 03DE, having a finite global presentation, is
-- `SheafOfModules.HasFiniteGlobalPresentation`: the two coproducts of the global presentation
-- are finite.
add_to_stacks 03DE "finite global presentation" SheafOfModules.HasFiniteGlobalPresentation

end
